Morocco","","text","",""]]},"KLTC":{"d":[["","TZ","iso","",""]]},"KQNK9":{"d":[["Distribution and Habits. Euselasia a. aurum inhabits the Pacific slope of Mexico from central Oaxaca north to Nayarit. It is found in a great variety of habitats from 900 to 2400 m, from the most humid cloud forest to dryer habitats such as semi evergreen forest, dry tropical forest, oak forest (Quercus) and pine-oak forest (Pinus – Quercus). It is found of perching along forested edges in the early afternoon, often in the company of Adelpha species. Euselasia aurantiaca aurantiaca ranges from Venezuela and Central America north to Chiapas and Veracruz on the Mexican Atlantic slope.","","text","",""]]},"KVVKL":{"d":[["Canada, USA (Nfld, south to Maine and NH); Finland, Great Britain (Scotland), Lithuania, Norway, Sweden; Russia: RUN (incl. Novaya Zemlya); Russia: WS, ES, FE (north Russia and central Asia: Novaya Zemlya, Murmanskaya oblast, Arkhangelskaya oblast, Komi Rep., Tyumenskaya oblast, Krasnoyarskiy kray, Irkutskaya oblast, Yakutiya, Magadan oblast, Kamchatka (incl. Bering Is), Amurskaya oblast); Mongolia.","","text","",""],["Eastpalaearctic","","text","",""],["Nearctic","","text","",""],["Westpalaearctic","","text","",""]]},"L2DXT":{"d":[["SE-Brazil (Rio de Janeiro)","","text","",""]]},"L2HPX":{"d":[["Namibia","","text","native",""]]},"L2WRG":{"d":[["Guadeloupean Exclusive Economic Zone","33177","mrgid","",""]]},"LQX3F":{"d":[["Distribution. So far known only from the type locality in Homhil area, Socotra, Yemen.","","text","",""]]},"LY5B2":{"d":[["Brazilian Exclusive Economic Zone","8464","mrgid","native",""]]},"MHYH8":{"d":[["North America","","text","",""]]},"MJ223":{"d":[["North America","","text","",""]]},"MMK63":{"d":[["CO","CO","iso","",""]]},"MRBM":{"d":[["Madagascar (Toliara)","","text","",""]]},"MWZWY":{"d":[["","BOR","tdwg","",""]]},"MYT4":{"d":[["MDG","MDG","tdwg","",""]]},"N8J3K":{"d":[["Gruziya","48468","mrgid","native",""]]},"N8T4":{"d":[["China (Sichuan)","","tex